[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m In genetic the reverse complement of a sequence is formed by **reversing** the sequence and then taking the complement of each symbol.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m The four nucleotides in DNA is Adenine (A), Cytosine (C), Guanine (G) and Thymine (Thymine). 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m - A is the complement of T 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m - C is the complement of G.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m This is a bi-directional relation so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m - T is the complement of A
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m - G is the complement of C.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m For this kata you need to complete the reverse complement function that take a DNA string and return the reverse complement string.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
