[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m [question] QUESTION:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m Americans are odd people: in their buildings, the first floor is actually the ground floor and there is no 13th floor (due to superstition).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m Write a function that given a floor in the american system returns the floor in the european system.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m With the 1st floor being replaced by the ground floor and the 13th floor being removed, the numbers move down to take their place. In case of above 13, they move down by two because there are two omitted numbers below them.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m Basements (negatives) stay the same as the universal level.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6902)[0m [More information here](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storey#European_scheme)
